DASH.glossary.hl={m:"Breadth",d:"New highs = NYSE stocks at a 52-week high; new lows = at a 52-week low. Index up while lows still dominate = a narrow bounce. Latest session (Thu 12 Nov): 39 highs vs 222 lows (WSJ), the most lows since 5 Nov and much worse than 45 vs 100 Wednesday, even though the S&P fell only 0.35% — rising yields hit small and rate-sensitive stocks while a few big names held the index up. Lows have beaten highs on every session in our chart this month except 4 Nov; more highs than lows again would be the first sign of healing."};

